From: Til Kaiser <mail@tk1454.de>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: validate USXGMII RX lock before trusting it

On AN7581, the shallow USXGMII PCS RX link status can report link up
while the BASE-R status still lacks block lock and RX link. In that
state the later USXGMII AN status reads as zero, so phylink never sees
the link even though the external PHY has copper link.

Treat that state like the existing bad-lock case: if the PMA still sees
RX signal, reset the CDR and let phylink poll again later.

Signed-off-by: Til Kaiser <mail@tk1454.de>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -2067,14 +2067,31 @@ static bool an7581_pcs_have_rx_signal(st
 	return count >= 4;
 }
 
+static bool an7581_pcs_usxgmii_has_block_lock(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
+					      int index)
+{
+	struct airoha_pcs_maps *maps = &priv->maps[index];
+	u32 base_r;
+
+	regmap_read(maps->usxgmii_pcs,
+		    AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_BASE_R_10GB_T_PCS_STUS_1, &base_r);
+
+	return (base_r & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_BLK_LK) &&
+	       (base_r & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_RX_LINK_STUS);
+}
+
 int an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv, int index)
 {
 	struct airoha_pcs_maps *maps = &priv->maps[index];
+	bool pcs_up;
 	u32 val;
 
-	/* Check if PCS is UP or Down */
+	/* Check if PCS is UP or Down. Also handle the partial-lock case
+	 * where PCS_STUS_1 reports RX link up, but BASE-R has no block lock.
+	 */
 	regmap_read(maps->usxgmii_pcs, AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_STUS_1, &val);
-	if (val & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_RX_LINK_STATUS_UP)
+	pcs_up = val & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_RX_LINK_STATUS_UP;
+	if (pcs_up && an7581_pcs_usxgmii_has_block_lock(priv, index))
 		return 0;
 
 	/* Validate if this is consistent with RX SigDet module */
